From 32ec5ec1f41665bbb0d2f243930894dd8d63abbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 13:53:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03995/11362] [outer-loop] Capture diagnostic: real lp85 L2
 reinduction fails because model rambles into engine() comments; fix =
 separate focused goal call (NOT a budget bump)

Captured the EXACT real lp85 L2 reinduction /completion call (proto_l2_capture.py tees the HTTP
layer; results/l2_capture.jsonl). Root cause, definitive + live-representative (live agent uses the
same max_tokens=2560, arc_competition_agent.py:2200): the real L2 prompt is 9290c (vs synthetic
~2200) with real click-action transitions; the model IGNORES "not even as comments" and rambles its
analysis into engine() comments, exhausts 2560 tokens (stop_type=limit), and NEVER writes
is_level_complete -> missing def -> proposer_failed. Deterministic, not variance.

Fix tested on the captured prompt (proto_l2_fix_finder.py / .json):
  B raise budget 2560->4096: FAILS (rambles to fill 4096, still no is_level_complete). Do NOT just
    bump max_tokens.
  C goal-first ordering: works (185 tok, both defs) but n=1.
  D separate focused goal-only call: works best (17 tok, 3.5s, valid). Structural -- engine ramble
    cannot starve a goal induced in its own call.

Recommended: D -- induce is_level_complete in a focused call (or as a fallback when the combined
induce yields a valid engine but missing/degenerate goal). Unblocks L2 reinduction so the
goal-repair loop + structural-alignment goal can run. Write-up appended to
docs/research-notes/l2-fixstack-measurement-2026-06-25.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
